# POST /verify: a receipt in, valid or not out
route     POST /verify
handler   verify
memo      the contract of POST /verify on tiesapi.com
input
  {"federated_id", "hash", "issued_at", "receipt", "label_sha256"}: the fields of a reply of POST /receipt
  label_sha256 for an entry receipt; left out for a v0 tie receipt
processing
  1 federated_id, hash, issued_at and receipt have their forms; label_sha256, when sent, is sha256:<64 hex>
  2 recompute the HMAC with the authority key over the same fields, and compare in constant time
output
  200 {valid: true | false, federated_id, hash, issued_at, label_sha256, attests}; 400 for a malformed field
  check: any change to one field gives valid: false
graph
  builds on receipt
example
  POST /receipt {"federated_id": "theisen-api:d030e7551d91b584", "line": "{\"n\":1,\"who\":\"theisen-api:d030e7551d91b584\",\"label\":\"https://tiesapi.com/catalog/sha256:5989aca695bc8d3a40aa3c35f5197e7e7eb14737f416535968d7e9f1faa42e7a\",\"inside\":\"sha256:5989aca695bc8d3a40aa3c35f5197e7e7eb14737f416535968d7e9f1faa42e7a\",\"parents\":[],\"memo\":\"example: line 1, the registration\",\"by\":\"human\",\"prev\":null,\"hash\":\"sha256:b984cebaf1ab8f2b29004acf928d9b5e7d48bf6ed84d93c29a1ac30cf84dfae2\"}"}
